## Setup All 5 Mine Sarthi Services — Dependency Installation & Launch

## Architecture Overview

The project is a full-stack IoT data pipeline:

```mermaid
graph LR
  A["Service 1: publisher_mqtt.py<br/>(IoT Simulator)"] -->|MQTT| B["Docker: Mosquitto<br/>(MQTT Broker :1883)"]
  B -->|MQTT| C["Service 3: consumer.py<br/>(MQTT→HTTP Bridge)"]
  C -->|HTTP POST| D["Service 2: fastapi_app.py<br/>(FastAPI Backend :8000)"]
  D -->|Write| E["Docker: InfluxDB :8086"]
  D -->|Write| F["Docker: PostgreSQL :5432"]
  G["Service 4: ML Service :8001"] -->|Read| E
  G -->|Read| F
  H["Service 5: Frontend :8080"] -->|WebSocket/API| D
  H -->|API| G
```

## Pre-requisite: Docker Infrastructure

The MQTT broker error (`WinError 10061 - Connection refused`) occurs because **Mosquitto, InfluxDB, and PostgreSQL** are not running. These are defined in [docker-compose.yml](file:///d:/Desktop/sih%202025/data%20pipeline/docker-compose.yml) and must be started first.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Docker Desktop must be **running** before we start. All 3 infrastructure services (Mosquitto, InfluxDB, PostgreSQL) will be spun up via `docker compose up -d`.

## Proposed Changes

### Step 1 — Start Docker Infrastructure
```bash
# From: d:\Desktop\sih 2025\data pipeline
docker compose up -d
```
This starts:
- **Mosquitto** (MQTT broker on `:1883`) — fixes the `WinError 10061`
- **InfluxDB** (time-series DB on `:8086`)
- **PostgreSQL** (relational DB on `:5432`, with [init.sql](file:///d:/Desktop/sih%202025/data%20pipeline/postgres/init.sql))

